Hair for the clay hm08 dummy
============================

MakeClothes (official):

  Hair is a *proxy* (clothes), not the helper. Each hair vertex follows
  three vertices on the helper or the body. The helper mesh is a fitting
  cage (helper-hair, helper-tights, …) and is not drawn.

  https://static.makehumancommunity.org/assets/creatingassets/makeclothes/introduction.html
  https://static.makehumancommunity.org/makehuman/docs/hairstyles_and_clothes.html

These OBJ files offset the hm08 *body* scalp/nape (CC0), a few centimetres
out. They are not the helper-hair cage (that looked like slabs over the face).

Bangs are a separate MHCLO in community packs. Here: bangs_brow / bangs_face
are a thin hairline strip, optional.
